Description: Tools for simulation, estimation, diagnostics, and exploratory
    analysis of multidimensional spatial and spatio-temporal point processes
    on hyperrectangular domains of any dimension. The package supports Poisson
    and marked Poisson point processes whose log-intensity combines
    coordinates, scalar and functional covariates, categorical and continuous
    marks, and smooth terms, fitted by a multidimensional extension of the
    Berman-Turner device (Baddeley and Turner (2000)
    <doi:10.1111/1467-842X.00128>); multidimensional inhomogeneous K-function
    estimators; residual and global-envelope diagnostics; log-Gaussian Cox
    processes (Moller et al. (1998) <doi:10.1111/1467-9469.00115>); and
    epidemic-type aftershock sequence models (Ogata (1998)
    <doi:10.1023/A:1003403601725>) with regression-based background
    intensities. The ETAS triggering routine is adapted from the 'Fortran'
    code of the 'etasFLP' package.
